This is how I play, so YMMV ..
My general advice is to play faster ... not type faster, but avoid in-
game detours.  The more turns that you play the more turns there are
to make a mistake, so just gather enough gear and go win.
For example:
1) I magic map and ^T across all of Gehennom that I can.  Even
ascending in under 40k turns there is nothing that I need to find in
Gehennom;
2) I usually skip the levels between Quest and Medusa, too;
3) one of my first actions after picking up the Orb of Fate is
levelporting back to the quest home level;
4) Don't worry about optimizing armor slots, for a Valk, just fully
enchant the first pair of gloves (other than fumbling, 'natch) that
you find ... voila! "Done, check that off of the list!"
5) the same goes for helmets, just enchant an elven leather helm,
it'll be fine;
6) don't bother with rust-proofing anything... boring;
7) ditto for spellcasting;
8) Another suggestion is to play on NAO, the place is filthy with dead
wizards and their starting cloaks :)
9) Don't worry about maximizing strength with the quest monsters (i.e.
you're engorged, but you have yet to maximize your strength, so never
mind the giant corpses lying around.  Sure, if you have a blessed
tinning kit, might as well use it, but don't go out of your way);
10) don't spend time on stashes ... you won't need much of that stuff
anyway.

